"notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p4), Total Government Funds column. Taxes 27,104,201 split into property 22,850,108, motor vehicle 2,462,729 and lodging 1,791,364 using Statement of Activities general receipts (p2); sum matches. Debt service 1,969,471 split into principal 1,695,000, interest 273,710 and admin fee 761 using the nonmajor combining totals (p14); sums to printed line. State 8,898,719 and Other 12,477,185 kept as printed (no breakdown for those lines; Other flagged review). Miscellaneous General 12,067,255 recorded as general government with review (GF misc plus ARPA). Beginning cash = beginning fund balances 20,682,234 (p4); ending 14,728,665. Identity: 20,682,234 + 50,447,854 - 56,401,423 + 3,119,626 - 3,119,626 = 14,728,665. Balance sheet from Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1), no liabilities. Detail: General Fund from the budgetary comparison schedule (pp5-8, departmental), Road, Inheritance Tax, Health Reserve and ARPA budgetary schedules (pp9-12), and the nonmajor combining schedule Totals column (p14; 14 funds so combined; p13 individual fund columns not recorded). Zero-amount lines mostly omitted. 'Operating expenses' lines use detail_category not itemized (catch-all object). Detail revenue/expenditure schedule actuals are budget-basis and the General fund and other major fund totals tie to p4 columns. Read pages 1-14 of 14."
